From: CubieBoard4 Build System <build@cubieboard4>
Date: Thu, 6 Mar 2026 14:18:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] dts: sun9i-a80-cb4: set WiFi pwrseq timing limits

Add post-power-on-delay-ms and cap max-frequency on the BCM4330
SDIO node to improve initialisation reliability.

The BCM4330 (AP6330) requires time after its reset line is released
before it can respond to SDIO commands. Without a delay the host
may attempt card enumeration before the chip is ready. A 1000 ms
post-power-on delay in the pwrseq-simple node ensures the chip is
stable before the first SDIO command is issued.

Capping max-frequency at 25 MHz keeps the SDIO clock within the
range tested to work reliably with the BCM4330 on this board.

Signed-off-by: CubieBoard4 Build System <build@cubieboard4>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun9i-a80-cubieboard4.dts | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun9i-a80-cubieboard4.dts2025-03-28 22:59:57.000000000 +0200
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun9i-a80-cubieboard4.dts2026-03-06 14:18:45.483031984 +0200
@@ -116,6 +116,7 @@
 compatible = "mmc-pwrseq-simple";
 clocks = <&ac100_rtc 1>;
 clock-names = "ext_clock";
+post-power-on-delay-ms = <1000>;
 /* enables internal regulator and de-asserts reset */
 reset-gpios = <&r_pio 0 2 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>; /* PL2 WL-PMU-EN */
 };
@@ -162,6 +163,7 @@
 vqmmc-supply = <&reg_cldo3>;
 mmc-pwrseq = <&wifi_pwrseq>;
 bus-width = <4>;
+max-frequency = <25000000>;
 non-removable;
 status = "okay";
 };
